\par 
                 EXPLANATORY NOTES FOR WRC107 CALCULATION\par 
                 ========================================\par 
\par 
              NOZZLE SUMMARY\par 
\par 
                 Calculated : YES/NO\par 
                 -------------------\par 
                 There may be various reasons for which a specific nozzle or attachement\par 
              needs not to be verified. In this case the option 'NO' appears.\par 
\par 
                 Method for the analysis\par 
                 -----------------------\par 
                 The procedures available include WRC107 for spheres and cylinders,\par 
               WRC297, and BS5500 app.G.\par 
\par 
                 Summation convention\par 
                 --------------------\par 
                 This option concerns the manner to combine the individual components of\par 
              the stress tensors connected with the pressure load and the external loads\par 
              in order to obtain the complete status of stress around the attachment.\par 
                 It is possible to use the WRC107 convention with the BS5500 analysis\par 
              method, and viceversa.\par 
\par 
                 Shear reduced to foot\par 
                 ---------------------\par 
\par 
                 When this option is selected, the external forces and moments given\par 
              in input are considered as applied to the nozzle end. Hence they are\par 
              transferred autoamtically to the nozzle-to-shell junction by conside-\par 
              ring the nozzle height as the lever arm.\par 
\par 
                 External loads\par 
                 --------------\par 
                 The used specification for standard nozzle loads, if any, is quoted.\par 

